Subject: CVE-2026-61485: Apache Lucy: Freezer/InStream deserialization bomb - unbounded allocation reading an index 
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

Severity: moderate 

Affected versions:

- Apache Lucy (Lucy): all versions

Description:

** UNSUPPORTED WHEN ASSIGNED ** Memory Allocation with Excessive Size Value vulnerability in Apache Lucy.

This issue affects Apache Lucy: all versions.

As this project is retired, we do not plan to release a version that fixes this issue. Users are recommended to find an alternative or restrict access to the instance to trusted users.

NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.

